{
  // GRA-172: tsconfig.json's `exclude` keeps src/testing/** and *.test.ts
  // out of the build on purpose — see that file's own comment — which means
  // "tsc --noEmit clean" has only ever been a claim about src/ minus those.
  // src/testing/ is not scaffolding any more: stripComments.ts is the shared
  // engine the ConnectionState guard (surface.test.ts) and the
  // PROTOCOL_VERSION drift scan (device.test.ts) both depend on, and neither
  // guard's own type checker sees it.
  //
  // This is a second, standalone project, not a patch to tsconfig.json, and
  // it does NOT cover "everything": it type-checks 15 of the 31 .ts files
  // under src/ — the build project's 13 non-test files plus the 2 under
  // src/testing/ (harness.ts, stripComments.ts) — with noEmit, so it can
  // never write to dist/ and can never change what `npm run build` or
  // `npm pack` produce. tsconfig.json keeps its existing exclusions
  // unchanged; the published package is unaffected by this file existing
  // at all. Confirm the boundary with `npx tsc -p tsconfig.typecheck.json
  // --listFilesOnly` rather than trusting this count as it drifts.
  //
  // *.test.ts (16 files) stays excluded here too, matching the build
  // project — not because it's out of scope in principle, but because this
  // ticket's own Owns line is mcp/tsconfig*.json, mcp/package.json and
  // .github/workflows/**, not the test files themselves. The first run of
  // this project (before this exclusion was added back) found 7 pre-existing
  // type errors, all vitest mock-typing mismatches in capture.test.ts and
  // cli.test.ts, none in src/testing/. Those are real and vitest's esbuild
  // transform has never caught them either — but fixing them is a separate,
  // wider change to files this ticket cannot touch. See GRA-172's Linear
  // comment for the full first-run output; flagged there for a follow-up
  // ticket rather than silently absorbed here.
  //
  // Naming note: the npm script for this is `typecheck:src`, not
  // `typecheck:all` — an earlier draft used "all" and a QA caught that a
  // type error appended to surface.test.ts (one of the 16 excluded files)
  // left it at exit 0 printing nothing. A name claiming full coverage it
  // doesn't have is exactly the defect class this ticket exists to fix one
  // level up; do not rename this back to "all" without actually covering
  // all 31 files (which reopens the capture.test.ts/cli.test.ts errors
  // above).
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts"],
  "exclude": ["src/**/*.test.ts"]
}
